YouTube PiP builds on ideas from decky-pip by Ross Squires (BSD-3-Clause),
https://github.com/rossimo/decky-pip :
  - showing a web page in a native Steam browser view (CreateBrowserView) over the game,
  - asking Steam for the "Notification" UI composition level so that view is drawn over the game,
  - reading the Steam menus' on-screen size so the window can stay out of their way.
The code in this repository is a new implementation; the approach and the composition-hook
lookup follow decky-pip. The QR encoder follows the structure of Project Nayuki's QR Code
generator library (MIT).

The cast receiver (ytpip_lounge.py, and the SSDP/DIAL discovery in main.py) is a new implementation of YouTube's
"Lounge" screen protocol and the DIAL discovery protocol. No code was copied; the protocol is documented by
open-source projects such as yt-cast-receiver (patrickkfkan) and plaincast.

